                 f"That ARM admits EXACTLY this shape — the staged set is "
                 f"{tid}'s own lifecycle records with the CARD among them — and it earns custody "
                 f"WITHOUT manufacturing authored work, because the REQUIRED `yitc-v2 audit post "
                 f"--task {tid} --commit <new>` grades the CUMULATIVE range: the already-audited "
                 f"ship AND this repair together, so the auditor receives strictly more than it did "
                 f"on the RED pass. It refuses if the staged set carries authored content (then drop "
                 f"--card-repair — THIS leg already admits you), and it refuses if the commit the RED "
                 f"verdict covers carries no authored content (then the card shipped nothing and "
                 f"route (3) is yours). A correction that instead rides a commit that ALSO carries "
                 f"authored work is equally fine, exactly as the mode-a cycle folds its superseded "
                 f"verdict alongside the fix; (3) the cause is "
                 f"OUTSIDE {tid}'s declared scope, is environmental, or has no shipping fix — STOP "
